  },
  {
   "claim": "Painted in London in 1533 (dated beneath the signature on the floor) by Hans Holbein the Younger",
   "source": "https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/hans-holbein-the-younger-the-ambassadors ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ambassadors_(Holbein)"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Left: Jean de Dinteville, French ambassador to the court of Henry VIII; right: his close friend Georges de Selve, Bishop of Lavaur; inscriptions give their ages as 29 and 25 (NG in-depth text: 28 and 24) — both under thirty",
   "source": "https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/hans-holbein-the-younger-the-ambassadors ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ambassadors_(Holbein)"
  },
  {
   "claim": "Between them: celestial and terrestrial globes, scientific instruments, books, and a lute with one broken string",
   "source": "https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/hans-holbein-the-younger-the-ambassadors ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ambassadors_(Holbein)"
  },
  {
   "claim": "The skull can only be seen properly if you look up at the painting from the bottom right corner",
   "source": "https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/hans-holbein-the-younger-the-ambassadors"
  },
  {
   "claim": "The skull is a deliberately distorted (anamorphic) image that only reads correctly from an oblique angle",
